<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτρα</span></b>  (A), 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήρ-τρη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτηρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>womb</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.108
			</span></i> (dub.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				91d
			</span></i>, etc.: also in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> l.c.: <i>the cervix including the orifice of the womb</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				510b14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a swine's
				<i>matrix</i>, reckoned a great dainty, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτρας τόμοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Telecl.
					1.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτραν . . πωλοῦσιν, ἥδιστον κρέας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					220
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ μήτρας . . ἀποθανεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					193
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.733e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.96f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>source, origin</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.46
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆτραι τῆς ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.441
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>core, heart-wood</i> of trees, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.6.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>diseased condition</i> of the wood, 'soft-wood', ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.7.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>queen-wasp</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐργάται</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				627b32
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. χελωνίων, χελωνίοις</span>,
			<i>bolts</i> for locks, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1028.20
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. θύρας</span>,
				=
			<i>repagulum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
